Revision history for Dist-Conformance

0.003 2026-11-06 TEODESIAN
    - DataSchema reads an INI file, such as dist.ini, as a hash of its
      sections by their whole header.  A key that a section repeats is the
      list of its values, as Dist::Zilla reads it.  A file whose name ends in
      .ini is read so by default, and format: ini says it for any other.
      So a flavor can refuse a key of a plugin, such as user under
      [GithubMeta].
    - New check SystemPackages: a repository declares the packages of the
      operating system that it needs in metamerge.yml.  x_system_packages
      names each dependency, with its package for each packager, a package
      for a distro or a release of one, and a test that must run once it is
      installed.  x_system_sources holds the third-party archives of deb,
      each with the full fingerprint of its signing key.  The check refuses
      a name that is not a plain package name, such as a deb name that ends
      in -, which apt reads as a removal, a source that is not declared,
      and an archive that nothing installs from.
      Dist::Conformance::Check::SystemPackages->declared returns the
      validated declaration of a snapshot or a directory, and ->resolve
      what one host installs, and which dependencies it cannot resolve.
      conformance packages prints the packages, tests, sources or needs for
      the host of /etc/os-release, for a shell script, and exits 2 when a
      dependency has no package for the host.
    - Dist::Conformance::Schema::refuse dies with the message of validate,
      for an error that a schema cannot express.

0.002 2026-11-04 TEODESIAN
    - CriticProfile compares the policies of the profile with those of its
      template, and fails with the name of each policy that the template
      enables and the profile neither enables nor turns off with [-Name].
      Before, it compared only the first line, so a profile kept passing
      after its template gained a policy.  The keys header and outdated are
      deprecated and ignored; a flavor that names them still loads.

0.001 2026-11-02 TEODESIAN
    - Initial Release
